Z||000020||chester||08-02-2001||12:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gragon:<BR><B>Chester,<P>I love your car, looks great.  Here are a couple of mine:<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks!  I like the look of your MR2 as well.  I always liked that body style. Is the red and black theme inside your doing or was that stock?  Looks great!<P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000021||Gragon||08-02-2001||12:12 PM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chester:<BR><B>Is the red and black theme inside your doing or was that stock?  Looks great!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Thanks for the compliment.  MKII interiors are very functional, but quite boring in my opinion.  It is like everything is black, no color.  I went on a mission to try to spice mine up but not to go overboard.  Custom leather seats and door panels, white faced gages with the dash surround painted red, aluminum dask kit riveted in place, A-piller mounted boost gage and fuel/air ratio gage, leather shift boot made from left over seat material, greddy shift knob, leather two tone steering wheel wrap, stainless steel door sill overlays.<P>Have you dynoed yours?  What kind of hp are you pushing?  Love the wheels......they bring out the lines in the Fiero nicely.<P> <IMG SRC="http://board.mr2pages.com/bulk/View04.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>91 MR2 Turbo<BR>89 MR2 SC<BR>01 PT Cruiser<P>[This message has been edited by Gragon (edited 08-02-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by Gragon (edited 08-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||chester||08-02-2001||01:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gragon:<BR><B>   [QUOTE]Originally posted by chester:<BR>[b]Is the red and black theme inside your doing or was that stock?  Looks great!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Thanks for the compliment.  MKII interiors are very functional, but quite boring in my opinion.  It is like everything is black, no color.  I went on a mission to try to spice mine up but not to go overboard.  Custom leather seats and door panels, white faced gages with the dash surround painted red, aluminum dask kit riveted in place, A-piller mounted boost gage and fuel/air ratio gage, leather shift boot made from left over seat material, greddy shift knob, leather two tone steering wheel wrap, stainless steel door sill overlays.<P>Have you dynoed yours?  What kind of hp are you pushing?  Love the wheels......they bring out the lines in the Fiero nicely.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://board.mr2pages.com/bulk/View04.jpg">  <P>[/B][/QUOTE]<P>The interior looks great.  I have some things left to do on my interior.  Something along the lines of your seats only grey and red with red piping.  I'll post some interior pics when I get home. Thanks for the compliment on the rims.  It took me 3 months and countless hours on the net to settle on those.  I have not dynoed the car as of yet cause I'm waiting on the $$$ to get a programable ECM and have it dyno tuned while I'm at it.  With what we did the guesstimate was 190-200 hp. A desktop dyno program came up with 215 with all the mods so the 190-200 hp is a pretty realistic figure.  I also have plans to turbo it with a small shot of nitrous, but I'm currently putting my extra cash into a project 4 seater that another Fiero forum member started. You can see it at  <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009012.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/009012.html</A>  . <P>||||reg||6
